-- title:
--   Igusa Gauss ring at ∞ cuts out R₀-integers (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a non-zero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ over $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ (the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(Nq)$) whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those rational affine geometric places at which the geometric $j$-value lies in the supersingular set. Assume $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ (as intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from the former to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map having the maximal ideal as kernel, compatible with $A\to\kappa$, with a degree-preserving place map and a divisor-pushforward property — subject to $(h_{R_0})$: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral, with $R_0$-residue equal to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Further data: a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$; families $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $O^{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$, subject to hypotheses summarised as follows: $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the point $\infty=[1:0]$ consists of the quotients $x/y$ of Laurent series over $A$ with non-zero reduction of $y$; $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective, each $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ is the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying $\infty$ to $\ell$ mod $q$, and pullback along any $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ permutes the family; each $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ meets $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in exactly $A$, is fixed by all these automorphisms, contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a\in A$, and lies over $R_0$ in the sense that an $R_0$-integral $f$ which is regular wherever $j$ is and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$ has its image in $O^{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, with $f-a$ in the maximal ideal whenever the residue of $a\in A$ is the value of the residue of $f$ at $s$. Then for every $f$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$: $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion form of the comparison between the level-$M'$ Gauss (constant) reduction and the Igusa Gauss valuation ring at the cusp $\infty$ of the full level $q^2M'$ tower: integrality for the constant reduction of $X_0(M')$ is detected by the Gauss ring at infinity upstairs. The case $q=3$ is recorded separately, and it feeds the construction of the semistable covering charts and their descent, being used in the statements about maximal ideals of the Drinfeld ring, smoothness over the base at good points of the two-chart integral model, and rationality of places of the floor trace.
